UID:10006599-1786284000-1786291200@www.ashevilleart.org
SUMMARY:Exhibition on Screen | John Singer Sargent: Fashion and Swagger
DESCRIPTION:JOHN SINGER SARGENT \nDirected by David Bickerstaff \nJohn Singer Sargent is known as the greatest portrait artist of his era. What made his ‘swagger’ portraits remarkable was his power over his sitters\, what they wore and how they were presented to the audience. Through interviews with curators\, contemporary fashionistas and style influencers\, Exhibition on Screen’s film will examine how Sargent’s unique practice has influenced modern art\, culture and fashion. \nFilmed at the Museum of Fine Arts\, Boston and the Tate Britain\, London\, the exhibition reveals Sargent’s power to express distinctive personalities\, power dynamics and gender identities during this fascinating period of cultural reinvention. Alongside 50 paintings by Sargent sit stunning items of clothing and accessories worn by his subjects\, drawing the audience into the artist’s studio. \nStep into the glittering world of fashion\, scandal and shameless self-promotion that made John Singer Sargent the painter who defined an era. \nExplore the unique creative process of the late 19th century’s favorite portrait artist and the way in which his portraits captured the spirit of a vibrant and rapidly changing age. \nPurchase Tickets \n  \nhttps://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/EOS-JS-Sargent-30sec-Trailer-v02-18CBR.mp4
URL:https://www.ashevilleart.org/event/exhibition-on-screen-john-singer-sargent/2026-08-09/
LOCATION:Asheville Art Museum\, 2 South Pack Square\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.ashevilleart.org/wp-content/uploads/EOS-John-Singer-Sargent_-Madame-X-Madame-Pierre-Gautreau-1883-84-oil-on-canvas-Sargent-John-Singer-1856-1925-scaled.jpg
GEO:35.5946714;-82.5512827
